More one-line patches.... 
The major problems seem to be coming from A) structures being allocated
but not initialized, and B) bugs in realloc() on the Sun. 

A) is my fault; my malloc / realloc zeros out the memory it returns, and
I was accidentally relying on that. The problem should be taken care of
by the patches below. For B), achamber@cs.weber.edu has gotten vast
improvement (on a Sun) by linking with -lbsdmalloc. 

If you've been having problems with the game, please send me mail and
tell me if these fixes help. Include the system/OS type, since that
seems to be relevant. 

(There's also a known bug: if you type a very long message with no
spaces, it can overflow the text window. This is ugly, but does not
affect play; type ctrl-L to redraw the screen.) 

When things look a little bit more stable, I'll make an actual patch
file and submit it to c.s.g. 

--Z 

